WEBVTT

01:35.720 --> 01:37.889
Here. Food and a change of clothes.

01:39.224 --> 01:40.642
You'll stand out dressed like that.

01:41.226 --> 01:42.143
Put those on.

01:48.775 --> 01:50.026
Is this a tunic?

01:50.110 --> 01:53.404
Yeah, and this is like a hakama.

01:53.488 --> 01:55.031
Also, here.

01:55.115 --> 01:56.908
We wear sandals like this down here.

01:57.992 --> 02:01.704
The small-time thug look
suits you, Senpai.

02:01.788 --> 02:03.248
And what are these?

02:03.331 --> 02:05.333
Surely you know what rice balls are.

02:06.000 --> 02:09.003
100% white rice?! No millet?!

02:09.087 --> 02:10.338
And this one's seaweed?!

02:11.047 --> 02:13.091
Are these not luxuries?!

02:14.676 --> 02:16.594
I guess it would be in that village.

02:16.678 --> 02:19.055
H-How does this thing work?

02:32.610 --> 02:33.611
Here.

02:41.578 --> 02:43.246
So good!

02:43.830 --> 02:45.582
How is this so good?

02:45.665 --> 02:47.000
Is this the food of the gods?

02:47.083 --> 02:48.626
It's that good, huh?

02:48.710 --> 02:50.920
Have this one, too. Eat up.

02:51.004 --> 02:53.339
What are you, his auntie?

02:55.925 --> 03:00.221
I wish Asa could eat this, too...

03:01.973 --> 03:03.683
Hey, Dera.

03:05.393 --> 03:06.519
What is this place?

03:06.603 --> 03:07.729
Oh, uh...

03:07.812 --> 03:10.356
It's called a rest stop.

03:10.440 --> 03:12.775
It's like a modern stage station.

03:12.859 --> 03:14.611
There are food shops and latrines inside.

03:15.194 --> 03:17.322
You can buy local souvenirs, too.

03:18.281 --> 03:19.908
I see, I see.

03:21.367 --> 03:22.869
Wanna check out the inside?

03:23.453 --> 03:26.789
No need. We'll stay with Yuru.

03:26.873 --> 03:29.626
Why don't you go eat?

03:30.293 --> 03:32.462
We'll keep an eye on Yuru.

03:34.172 --> 03:36.341
In that case, don't mind if we do.

03:36.424 --> 03:38.593
- Let's go eat, Hana-chan.
- Yes, sir.

03:39.177 --> 03:41.721
Don't touch the driver's seat, okay?

03:41.804 --> 03:45.183
Do you not need to feed the horses inside?

03:45.266 --> 03:47.101
We'll feed them oil later.

03:56.736 --> 03:58.488
How much did you tell him?

03:58.571 --> 04:04.786
Well, when I told him that girl
wasn't his sister, he lost his mind.

04:04.869 --> 04:07.497
It's better not to say more.

04:07.580 --> 04:09.332
You're so nice.

04:09.958 --> 04:12.168
He's still just a kid.

04:12.252 --> 04:15.338
I wouldn't understand
since I don't like kids.

04:16.464 --> 04:17.715
Thanks for the meal.

04:18.299 --> 04:20.885
So, what do we do now?

04:20.969 --> 04:23.680
Take you two to your place?

04:23.763 --> 04:27.600
Nah, they know my face and name now.

04:27.684 --> 04:30.103
I'm ditching that spot.

04:30.186 --> 04:32.981
So you're homeless and caring
for someone else's child.

04:33.064 --> 04:34.232
Sounds rough.

04:35.525 --> 04:38.194
This is your problem, too.

04:38.278 --> 04:41.614
As a Higashi Village Daemon
retainer, you'll be helping me.

04:41.698 --> 04:45.493
I mean, I'll do what I can.

04:45.576 --> 04:46.703
All right.

04:46.786 --> 04:49.122
Then let's get married, Hana-chan.

04:52.542 --> 04:54.544
Our wedding rings.

04:54.627 --> 04:56.963
Do you always carry that around?

04:57.046 --> 05:00.258
Why do I have to marry you?!

05:02.176 --> 05:03.594
It wouldn't be for real.

05:03.678 --> 05:07.849
We have to blend in with society
so we can protect Yuru.

05:07.932 --> 05:10.852
Rumors about outsiders spread
like wildfire in the country,

05:10.935 --> 05:13.146
so we need a decently big city.

05:13.730 --> 05:16.691
But I'm not confident I can do it alone.

05:16.774 --> 05:19.319
We don't have to get married to do that!

05:19.402 --> 05:20.611
We could be roommates!

05:21.279 --> 05:23.364
It's easier to rent a house as a family.

05:23.448 --> 05:25.575
People trust families way more, you know.

05:25.658 --> 05:31.331
Then I could be Yuru-kun's
much older sister!

05:31.414 --> 05:34.000
You could be our single father!

05:34.083 --> 05:37.795
A dad whose wife dumped the
kids on him and ran away?

05:37.879 --> 05:39.213
I heard his wife left him.

05:39.297 --> 05:42.175
Oh my. Was it domestic
violence or cheating?

05:42.925 --> 05:47.305
A heroic dad raising his kids
alone after his wife passed?

05:47.388 --> 05:49.098
Poor thing.

05:49.182 --> 05:50.475
Must be tough.

05:50.558 --> 05:52.310
Let's help him if he needs anything.

05:52.894 --> 05:57.315
Either way, it'd attract rumors and
attention among the neighbors.

05:57.982 --> 06:02.403
We'll go with Yuru's my kid,
and I remarried a younger woman.

06:02.487 --> 06:04.614
That's just our story, okay?

06:04.697 --> 06:05.948
Thanks for understanding.

06:06.032 --> 06:07.992
I never said yes.

06:08.493 --> 06:10.453
So, who's the head of the household?
Whose surname are we using?

06:11.120 --> 06:11.996
Well?

06:13.289 --> 06:14.916
No!

06:14.999 --> 06:20.296
I've already decided that
I'm marrying Jason Statham!

06:23.591 --> 06:26.636
Where do they keep the horses
inside this little box?

06:26.719 --> 06:29.514
The modern world below's
technology is amazing.

06:30.723 --> 06:32.225
Forgive me, Left and Right.

06:32.809 --> 06:34.894
I'm hogging all the food.

06:34.977 --> 06:36.687
Aren't you hungry?

06:37.355 --> 06:40.024
Our new master is nice.

06:40.108 --> 06:41.400
Don't worry about us.

06:41.484 --> 06:43.903
We don't eat human food.

06:45.113 --> 06:49.033
So, um... what should I call you?

06:49.117 --> 06:50.535
Whatever you want.

06:50.618 --> 06:52.662
You could even give us new names.

06:54.914 --> 06:57.500
Lord Right and Lady Left?

06:58.376 --> 07:00.294
That's so uptight.

07:00.378 --> 07:02.630
You're our master.

07:02.713 --> 07:04.340
You don't need to be so formal.

07:05.007 --> 07:06.092
Then...

07:07.844 --> 07:10.596
Right and Left.

07:12.098 --> 07:13.349
Let's cut to the chase.

07:13.433 --> 07:16.227
Tell me everything you know
about me and my sister.

07:21.691 --> 07:26.654
Let me start by sayin'
we sat at the entrance

07:27.155 --> 07:30.158
to Higashi Village for 400 years.

07:30.908 --> 07:33.327
We only saw the people who came and went.

07:33.828 --> 07:36.914
We don't know much
about what happened inside the village.

07:37.748 --> 07:40.918
The villagers mentioned
that twins had been born,

07:41.627 --> 07:44.881
and we started seeing you after some time.

07:47.258 --> 07:52.221
Your father used to take you huntin'
when you were a little thing.

07:52.305 --> 07:53.139
Yeah.

07:53.639 --> 07:57.310
My earliest memories
are of him teaching me to hunt.

07:57.393 --> 08:01.439
But we hardly ever saw the other twin.

08:02.064 --> 08:07.820
We assumed she'd died of an illness
or something shortly after her birth.

08:07.904 --> 08:10.531
But about ten years ago...

08:24.629 --> 08:29.509
we saw your parents flee
the village with a girl.

08:30.218 --> 08:34.138
She was a little girl,
with blood that smelled just like yours.

08:38.267 --> 08:42.146
And that little girl grew up
and attacked the village.

08:43.356 --> 08:48.528
I thought our parents
left both of us behind.

08:51.948 --> 08:54.242
But it was only me.

09:03.751 --> 09:10.383
Which means the self-proclaimed "real"
Asa might know where our parents are.

09:11.717 --> 09:14.387
Okay. Okay!

09:15.846 --> 09:17.139
Thanks for waiting.

09:19.642 --> 09:21.352
What is it, Hana-san?

09:22.019 --> 09:25.523
For reasons, we're going
to be your guardians.

09:25.606 --> 09:26.941
We appreciate your understanding.

09:27.567 --> 09:28.401
Guardians?

09:28.484 --> 09:31.988
We're responsible
if you ever get into trouble.

09:32.071 --> 09:34.907
By the way, Yuru,
we'll be riding for a while.

09:34.991 --> 09:36.742
Do you need to use the latrine?

09:36.826 --> 09:38.828
No. I just went over there.

09:38.911 --> 09:40.621
He's already getting into trouble!

09:40.705 --> 09:43.916
Also, don't sit on top of the car.

09:44.000 --> 09:45.167
You'll attract attention.

09:45.251 --> 09:46.586
Should I not?

09:47.336 --> 09:49.672
Right and Left have been sitting up there.

09:49.755 --> 09:52.842
Normal humans can't see Daemons.

09:52.925 --> 09:54.010
They can't?

09:54.093 --> 09:57.680
Daemon Wielders like you can see us.

09:57.763 --> 10:03.060
And Daemons can make ourselves
visible to certain humans.

10:03.144 --> 10:07.148
Finally, some people just happen
to possess the ability to see us.

10:08.524 --> 10:10.109
What's wrong?

10:10.192 --> 10:11.902
What are you barking at?

10:17.825 --> 10:19.869
The Kagemori clan, was it?

10:20.703 --> 10:22.872
Are they Daemon Wielders?

10:22.955 --> 10:25.875
Yeah, they've got a few.

10:25.958 --> 10:27.335
What are they like?

10:27.418 --> 10:29.545
They're a pain in the ass.

10:29.629 --> 10:33.007
They left Higashi Village and established
themselves in the world below.

10:33.674 --> 10:36.427
They're like a branch clan of the village.

10:37.053 --> 10:40.556
They left the village
over differences in opinion.

10:40.640 --> 10:43.809
Honestly, I'd rather not
get involved with them.

10:43.893 --> 10:48.105
In the world below, there's a network—

10:48.189 --> 10:51.025
uh, a web of former
Higashi Village people.

10:51.108 --> 10:56.781
For a while, we'd heard rumors that one
of the twins was with the Kagemoris.

10:57.782 --> 10:59.909
And that turned out to be true.

11:38.280 --> 11:39.824
Come on, come on.

11:45.204 --> 11:47.123
Come on, close faster.

11:53.879 --> 11:55.506
Aoi-chan.

11:56.257 --> 11:57.800
Why are you running from me?

11:59.009 --> 12:00.719
No! Stay away!

12:00.803 --> 12:03.347
Yeah, but...

12:04.557 --> 12:07.643
I need to get closer to kill you.

12:11.772 --> 12:12.773
Stay away.

12:13.399 --> 12:14.608
Stay back.

12:15.443 --> 12:18.612
If you come any closer...

12:22.533 --> 12:27.204
you'll step into my territory.

12:35.004 --> 12:38.549
Hello, Aoi-san? It's Jin.

12:39.550 --> 12:42.595
I've resolved the matter
with your stalker.

12:47.266 --> 12:51.187
I made him promise to never
come near you again.

12:52.730 --> 12:55.107
You can go back to work now.

12:56.942 --> 12:59.987
I'll notify the owner later.

13:02.406 --> 13:03.866
Good work.

13:32.394 --> 13:33.562
Miss.

13:36.649 --> 13:38.317
You can see them?

13:41.362 --> 13:43.280
Uh...

13:48.494 --> 13:49.620
Don't tell anyone.

13:52.039 --> 13:55.751
Hana-chan and I haven't
been told much either.

13:55.834 --> 13:58.879
Our families have lived
down here for generations.

13:58.963 --> 14:01.423
We just inherited this job
from our predecessors.

14:01.507 --> 14:05.928
Granny Yamaha only insisted that no
outsiders learn where Higashi Village is

14:06.011 --> 14:11.433
and that you twins not fall
into anyone else's hands.

14:12.518 --> 14:15.271
I procure goods and relay information.

14:15.354 --> 14:18.107
And I do odd jobs down here.

14:18.190 --> 14:20.317
I've never been to the village.

14:20.401 --> 14:23.487
I don't know what Granny
and the elders are thinking,

14:23.571 --> 14:26.949
but as a Tadera,
I have to respect the clan's rules.

14:29.577 --> 14:33.873
My real name's Tadera Ryu,
but you can keep calling me Dera.

14:35.124 --> 14:39.879
Granny seemed upset
about them trying to take me.

14:40.462 --> 14:43.632
She made that clear with you, too.

14:45.885 --> 14:48.387
What exactly are my sister and I?

14:51.473 --> 14:54.435
When a twin boy and girl are
born in a village to the east

14:54.518 --> 15:00.482
on a day when day and night are equal,
the world will be torn apart.

15:00.983 --> 15:06.906
As far as we know, the last time
that happened was 400 years ago.

15:07.740 --> 15:11.577
Twins dividing the day and night
were born in that village.

15:12.077 --> 15:15.831
During that era, the nation was split
into east and west in a major war.

15:16.332 --> 15:20.920
Before that, the nation was split
into north and south by another war.

15:21.462 --> 15:25.549
In both cases, Daemon Wielders
were involved behind the scenes.

15:26.175 --> 15:29.803
So we're cursed children who will
throw the world into chaos?

15:29.887 --> 15:35.142
No. It's the people who want to use
your power who start the fighting.

15:35.225 --> 15:36.644
Our power?

15:36.727 --> 15:38.395
I don't have any special powers.

15:38.479 --> 15:39.897
Not yet.

15:39.980 --> 15:44.068
You have the capacity to gain power.

15:44.151 --> 15:47.988
And Asa has probably already acquired it.

15:49.406 --> 15:53.243
That was "Break," wasn't it?

15:55.454 --> 16:00.626
"Break" is the power
to forcibly unravel anything.

16:00.709 --> 16:05.297
It easily forces anything open, whether
it's a powerful barrier or something else.

16:05.798 --> 16:08.759
Its twin is "Seal,"

16:08.842 --> 16:13.013
the power to forcibly close anything.

16:13.889 --> 16:17.351
What happens when "Break"
and "Seal" collide?

16:17.434 --> 16:18.852
A paradox.

16:19.603 --> 16:22.356
Has anyone ever acquired
both powers at once?

16:22.940 --> 16:25.609
Not as far as we know.

16:25.693 --> 16:29.697
Which means nobody knows
what would happen.

16:29.780 --> 16:32.741
Is it possible that rumors
about "something" happening

16:32.825 --> 16:36.370
have taken on a life of their own,
and the villagers are being manipulated?

16:37.204 --> 16:41.041
Come to think of it, there was a barrier
around the village, too.

16:41.125 --> 16:43.419
How did you come and go, Dera-san?

16:44.003 --> 16:47.172
There's a specific route to get through.

16:47.256 --> 16:50.467
"Go counterclockwise around these rocks
a certain number of times."

16:50.968 --> 16:55.639
"Go right at this crossroads, turn back
at the next, and go through the valley."

16:56.140 --> 16:59.810
"Make a 90-degree turn at this big tree."

16:59.893 --> 17:01.687
It's a real pain in the ass.

17:02.438 --> 17:08.694
My clan knows the route, so I can freely
pass through Higashi Village's barrier.

17:09.278 --> 17:14.742
Your mother is from down here and
stumbled upon that route to the village.

17:17.911 --> 17:18.954
It happens every once in a while.

17:19.997 --> 17:24.543
While lost and wandering,
some people happen upon the village.

17:41.393 --> 17:42.478
Yuru,

17:43.437 --> 17:49.234
in the place where I was born and raised,
your name means "night."

17:50.611 --> 17:56.992
Someday I hope I can take you,
your father, and Asa there.

18:23.727 --> 18:28.023
Flush when you're done.

18:28.607 --> 18:30.025
Wash your hands.

18:34.029 --> 18:38.033
I don't like these loud things
that roar like dragons.

18:38.659 --> 18:41.286
Extinguish the lights
in any room you're not using.

18:42.913 --> 18:46.959
Okay. I've learned all the rules
to using the latrine in the world below.

18:51.713 --> 18:55.676
Anyway, it's amazing that they don't
have to draw water from a well.

18:55.759 --> 18:59.721
And how does pushin' those
clicky things make light?

18:59.805 --> 19:03.183
And there are so many lights
in the city at night.

19:03.684 --> 19:07.354
I'm surprised
by all the tall stone castles, too.

19:07.437 --> 19:10.399
How many lords do they have down here?

19:10.482 --> 19:12.693
They're not castles, they're homes.

19:13.360 --> 19:17.156
Dera-san said dozens of people
live inside each one.

19:17.239 --> 19:19.741
There are so many more
people in the capital.

19:19.825 --> 19:22.202
Actually, this isn't the capital.

19:22.286 --> 19:26.582
He said in "Toh-kyo," the capital,
there are ten million people.

19:26.665 --> 19:29.585
Ten million?! How much rice
do all those people need?

19:30.252 --> 19:34.882
You mean this isn't the capital
despite all the people living here?

19:34.965 --> 19:37.551
I forget what this place was called.

19:38.051 --> 19:39.845
Hana-san told me.

19:40.846 --> 19:42.055
Guntama Prefecture?

19:42.139 --> 19:44.349
Guntama Prefecture. I'll remember that.

19:44.433 --> 19:49.146
Well, it'll certainly be easy to hide
with this many humans around.

19:49.229 --> 19:51.356
The best place to hide
a tree is the forest.

19:51.440 --> 19:56.987
And amongst all of these humans,
you're going to find your sister.

19:59.239 --> 20:00.073
Yeah.

20:01.074 --> 20:03.869
Dera-san and Hana-san
are probably good people.

20:05.078 --> 20:08.665
But if they're connected to the deception

20:08.749 --> 20:11.960
about my sister and the villagers
who kept that secret,

20:12.044 --> 20:14.046
I can't trust them completely.

20:14.588 --> 20:19.218
That said, I can't trust the woman
who calls herself Asa either.

20:24.765 --> 20:29.186
Fleeing the village with a child
was no small decision.

20:30.145 --> 20:31.897
I want to talk to them in person.

20:32.481 --> 20:36.693
I'll capture that Asa
and make her take me to Father and Mother.

20:37.319 --> 20:39.696
Will you help me, Left and Right?

20:40.280 --> 20:41.698
So we're looking for someone in this world

20:41.782 --> 20:43.700
where we don't know
our right from our left.

20:44.368 --> 20:47.663
Interesting! We haven't gotten
to kill time like this in 400 years.

20:48.330 --> 20:49.706
Let's enjoy this.

20:49.790 --> 20:54.044
You shouldn't say that when our master
is serious about this, Right.

20:54.127 --> 20:57.047
Well, how do you feel about it, Left?

21:00.968 --> 21:02.302
I don't like being chased.

21:02.970 --> 21:05.305
It's my nature to do the chasing.

21:07.891 --> 21:11.311
Yeah, yeah. Got it. Thanks.

21:12.354 --> 21:14.064
Hey, welcome back.

21:14.147 --> 21:15.190
I have returned.

21:15.274 --> 21:17.150
Hana-chan called.

21:17.234 --> 21:19.319
She found a place for us to live.

21:19.903 --> 21:22.406
We don't have to live
out of the car anymore.

21:24.491 --> 21:26.827
By the way, you use that thing often.

21:27.411 --> 21:28.328
What is that?

21:28.412 --> 21:29.371
This?

21:31.331 --> 21:34.001
I guess you wouldn't know what a phone is.

21:34.501 --> 21:37.796
It's for sending messages like
a smoke signal with letters or your voice?

21:37.879 --> 21:39.589
No, not quite...

21:40.173 --> 21:42.217
Anyway, that's what it does.

21:43.093 --> 21:44.428
I see.

21:44.511 --> 21:46.471
Something like a smoke signal.

21:47.472 --> 21:48.515
Got it.

21:50.559 --> 21:53.061
These guys really will accept anything.

23:27.572 --> 23:28.865
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

23:29.616 --> 23:32.869
Let me introduce you.
This is Kotetsu, and this is Jiro.

23:33.703 --> 23:36.248
Right! When you use the latrine,
before you leave...

23:36.331 --> 23:37.874
Extinguish the lights!
